verview": "Republican incumbent Bob Onder seeks a full term in Missouri's 3rd District after winning the August primary, setting up a rematch with Democrat Bethany Mann. The district leans Republican by about 13 points, and Onder holds a decisive financial advantage, with roughly $950,000 raised and $471,000 on hand compared with Mann's $43,000 raised and under $3,000 in cash. Outside spending has been negligible on both sides.\n\nPrediction markets give Onder about a 94% chance of winning, and no general-election polls show the race competitive. The redrawn congressional map that Republicans sought was blocked by the Supreme Court, but the seat remains firmly in Republican territory. Onder has also emphasized bipartisan work on healthcare legislation. All available evidence points to a safe Republican hold in November.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0408, "margin": -11.57}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0449, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0401, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0264, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0197, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0267, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.0276, "margin": -16.0}]}